# Copy these into Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
# (Production), then REDEPLOY -- variables only apply to deployments made after
# they were saved. Without all three, the Dealer and Contact forms in
# PRODUCTION show a "please call or email us" message instead of pretending to
# submit. (Previews/local dev log the submission and show success.)
#
# To try it locally, put the same three lines in .env.local (git-ignored),
# run `npm run dev` and submit the Contact form.
# Full walkthrough: README.md -> "Form delivery".

# Resend API key (https://resend.com) -- server-side only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Create it under API Keys with "Sending access" limited to your domain.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Where submissions are emailed. Comma-separate for several recipients.
LEAD_TO_EMAIL=

# Sender. Must be on a domain verified in Resend. Resend recommends a sending
# subdomain so it stays separate from your normal mailboxes, e.g.
# LEAD_FROM_EMAIL="SSS Website <website@mail.ssswheels.com.au>"
# (Before a domain is verified Resend only lets you send test emails to your own
# account address -- see the README for a no-DNS first test.)
LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=
